# CATEGORY: recurrence-loops / refractory rate-limiter candidate
# CLAIM: a stateful one-bit admission gate that accepts only rising-edge requests.
#
# Stream mapping:
#   i1 = request pulse for a scarce/disaster-sensitive action
#   o1 = admitted pulse
#
# Contract:
#   o1[t] = i1[t] & ~i1[t-1]
#
# The output is accepted only when the current request is present and the prior
# input was absent. In both supported Tau builds, the t<0 history for this
# input-lag pattern behaves fail-closed for a high first input, so the gate
# requires one observed quiet step before the first accept. A continuously high
# request stream is rejected until a quiet step rearms the gate.
#
# This is a candidate, not a recommended spec yet. Promotion should wait until
# the recommended Tau proof-plan registry is clean and can assign a profile/rule
# without increasing semantic-view drift.
set charvar off

always
  (o1[t]:sbf = (i1[t]:sbf & (i1[t-1]:sbf)')).
end
